            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0861" n="785" xml:id="pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.544/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-22T15:00:00-04:00">June 22, 1935—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Since instruction No. 3004 of May 29 last was sent, the Department has
                    received several additional protests from naturalized Americans of Swiss origin
                    residing in this country who have been called upon to pay Swiss military service
                    taxes. In discussing this matter with the Swiss authorities, endeavor to
                    ascertain definitely what objections are found to the proposals for a
                    nationality convention submitted with instruction No. 1521 of August 11, 1931.
                    It is deemed most desirable to reach a satisfactory agreement on this
                    subject.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
